# Template for Android release signing.
#
#   mkdir -p androidApp/keystore
#   cp androidApp/keystore.properties.example androidApp/keystore/keystore.properties
#
# Then fill in the real values below. The whole `androidApp/keystore/` directory is
# git-ignored, so anything you put in it — this file, the .jks itself — is covered. This
# example lives outside that directory precisely so it CAN be tracked; never put real values
# in it. The repository is public.
#
# Create the upload key first (keytool prompts for the passwords and your details):
#
#   keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore androidApp/keystore/cycluna-release.jks \
#     -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000 -alias cycluna
#
# Back that .jks up somewhere durable. With Play App Signing enabled this is only the
# *upload* key, so Google can reset it if it is lost; without Play App Signing, losing it
# means the listing can never be updated again.
#
# Absolute path — a relative one resolves against the Gradle module, not your shell.
storeFile=/Users/you/cycluna-app/androidApp/keystore/cycluna-release.jks
storePassword=
keyAlias=cycluna
keyPassword=
